    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0803" n="789" xml:id="pg789"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoar, Attorney-General, to Mr. Pierrepont, district
                        attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 17,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Spanish minister writes to the State
                    Department that an armed expedition for Cuba is fitting out in New York, to sail
                    in a day or two. You will please to use all efforts to prevent it, and instruct
                    the marshal to do the same.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. R. HOAR,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Pierrepont</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Attorney, New York.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
